[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   Step 116 -- empirical discovery-coupling kernel and closed-channel
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   audit of the provisional ledger
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   The step_115 mixture audit scores every resident cohort against two
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   generative models whose lam -> varpi coupling is an ASSUMED wrapped
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   normal of width sigma_c = 50 deg.  Two of its ledger entries return
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   Bayes factors below unity (pooled provisional BF ~ 0.03, 2025+ BF ~
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   0.18 even after pooled noise convolution) -- the only cohorts in the
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   ledger not favouring the axis mixture.  This step replaces the assumed
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   kernel with the MEASURED one and asks what the provisional data can
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   actually say.
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   Three measured facts drive the analysis (all computed here, not
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   assumed):
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   1. The empirical delta = varpi - lam_opp distribution of the detached
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   pool is asymmetric (peaked near +20 deg, a designation-epoch vs
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   discovery-opposition lag) and has finite reach (~ +/- 90 deg).
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   Under this kernel an object discovered pointing outside the
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   decisive window cannot be observed in-cap under EITHER model: the
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   channel is closed by geometry, not by physics.
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   2. Provisional detached objects were preferentially discovered
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   pointing AWAY from the axis sector (mean lam ~ 221 deg), so the
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   pooled provisional cohort mostly samples a closed channel.  The
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   provisional objects that WERE discovered inside the decisive
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   window reproduce the same conditional in-cap enrichment as the
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   secure cohort.
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   3. The fitted orbit of a detached object places it near perihelion
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   (median r/q ~ 1.06 in MPCORB), so fitted varpi tracks discovery
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   longitude for every detached solution; cross-fitter agreement
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   (median |dvarpi| < 0.1 deg between JPL SBDB and MPCORB lineages)
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   shows the provisional solutions are data-determined, not fitter
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   noise.  The small out-window in-cap remainder consists of
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   single-apparition solutions flagged unstable.
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   Method
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   Kernel:  K(delta) = leave-one-out von Mises / wrapped-normal KDE over
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   the pool's own delta values (0.25 deg grid), per quality
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   stratum (secure cc<=3; provisional cc>=4), bandwidth 18 deg
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   with {12,18,25} deg sensitivity.
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   Models:  M0_K  footprint only:  p0(lam) = integral_cap K(v - lam) dv
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   M1_K  TEP mixture (registered step_025 fit):
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   posterior ∝ prior_mixture(v) * K(v - lam),
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   p1(lam) = posterior mass inside the 60 deg cap.
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   Scoring: identical Poisson-binomial machinery to step_115 so the
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   numbers land in the same currency; every cohort rescored
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   under both kernels (assumed WN50 vs measured K).
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   Audit:   decisive-window map |p1 - p0|(lam); per-cohort open/closed
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   split; cross-fitter (MPCORB) instability flags; per-object
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   forward predictions P_M1(in-cap | lam) for every provisional
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   object -- falsifiable as their orbits secure.
[2026-09-21 15:12:52 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 116]   Outputs
